From 2be3d29de3c6b359cced1990db75d3b12b5b1f6f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 18:21:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Mac HDR export round 5: SDR edits compose in BT.709, the
 compositor alone places SDR in HLG

Mac run 587: source frames reached the compositor already converted to BT.2020 / HLG by AVFoundation (the video composition
was set to HLG), the first one hotter (frames 0-2 at 60 fps). Now an edit whose sources are all SDR sets the composition to
BT.709, so AVFoundation hands over the decoder's frames as they are and Core Image does the only SDR to HLG conversion, the
same way on every frame; an edit with an HDR source keeps BT.2020 / HLG. The writer pump tags every frame BT.2020 / HLG right
before the encoder (and traces what it got). Dolby Vision check scans 30 samples and lists NAL types. mac.yml: the HDR colour
step comes after the other checks so its failure doesn't skip them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Py2rxoCcw28R6FBjPPp318
